Fixed #1019 and committed it as 5fdccc10. Build, clippy with -D warnings, the format check and the full cargo test all pass.

The bug: for any model without a preset, the OpenAI-compatible path passed the 4096 request default to the warning as if it were the model's maximum. So --max-tokens 16000 on ollama, groq or openrouter told users to "lower to 4096". On gpt-6.1-sol that contradicted the other startup note, which tells them to raise it.

The fix (src/agent_builder.rs): openai_compat_output_ceiling now returns no ceiling at all unless a preset declares a real maximum, and with no ceiling the warning doesn't run. Before editing, I checked what each provider's yoagent constructor declares:
• **Keep a ceiling:** the GPT-6 presets on openai (128000) and DeepSeek's preset (384000, as #943 already treats it).
• **No ceiling now:** every other provider (openrouter, xai, groq, mistral, cerebras, github, ollama, zai, minimax, custom, unknown providers, and openai ids without a preset). All of them carry a 4096 default, not a maximum.

Checked with the built binary:
• ollama `llama3.3 at 16000 and gpt-6.1-sol` at 64000: no warning.
• `gpt-6-sol` at 200000: still warns and names 128000.

Tests (in src/openai_preset_tests.rs, built the same way the real code path builds them):
• Seven no-maximum rows return no warning. Each first checks that the old code would have warned.
• The `gpt-6-sol` warning is checked against the full expected string, with 128000 and 64000 as rows that must stay silent.
• DeepSeek still warns above 384000.
• When I put the old fallback back, the two no-maximum tests failed by name; with the fix restored they pass.

Things to know:
• I had to change three existing assertions: they expected the 4096 fallback, which was the bug. They now expect no ceiling. The Anthropic tests from #964 are untouched.
• `agent_builder.rs` ended up 2 lines shorter. It sits only 3 lines under its size-gate limit, so the new tests went in the sibling test file.
• My own loop runs provider=anthropic, so this change doesn't affect it.
• The Google and Bedrock paths still compare against their config's max_tokens, and Bedrock's is a 16K default. That looks like the same bug, but I haven't confirmed it with the binary. I filed it as #1020 rather than widen this task.
• No docs mention this warning, so there were no doc changes.
